# Lemon Blueberry Cupcakes

Based on [https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/lemon-blueberry-cupcakes](https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/lemon-blueberry-cupcakes)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Cupcakes

- [ ] 1.5 cups [all-purpose flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" } (spooned & leveled)
- [ ] 2 tsp [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup (8 Tbsps) [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }, softened to room temperature
- [ ] 1 cup [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [lemon zest]{ ing="lemon-zest" }
- [ ] 2 large [eggs]{ ing="egg" }, at room temperature
- [ ] 1.5 tsp [pure vanilla extract]{ ing="pure-vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [whole milk]{ ing="whole-milk" } or buttermilk, at room temperature
- [ ] 1/4 cup fresh [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }
- [ ] 1 cup fresh or [frozen blueberries]{ ing="frozen-blueberries" }, tossed in 1 Tbsp flour

### Cream Cheese Frosting

- [ ] 8 ounces [full-fat brick cream cheese]{ ing="full-fat-brick-cream-cheese" }, softened to room temperature
- [ ] 1/4 cup (4 Tbsps) [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }, softened to room temperature
- [ ] 2 cups [confectioners’ sugar]{ ing="confectioners-sugar" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [pure vanilla extract]{ ing="pure-vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] Pinch [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] Optional garnish: [lemon slices]{ ing="lemon-slices" } and extra [blueberries]{ ing="blueberries" }

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350°F (177°C). Line a 12-cup muffin pan with cupcake liners. This recipe yields approximately 15 cupcakes.
1. Whisk together [flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }, [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" } in a large bowl. Set aside.
1. Using a handheld or stand mixer with a paddle attachment, beat [butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }, [sugar]{ ing="confectioners-sugar" }, and [lemon zest]{ ing="lemon-zest" } on medium-high speed until creamed (about 3 minutes). Scrape bowl sides as needed. Add [eggs]{ ing="egg" } and [vanilla extract]{ ing="pure-vanilla-extract" }, beating about 1 minute. Add dry ingredients on low speed, slowly pour in [milk]{ ing="whole-milk" } and [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, and beat until just combined. Fold in the flour-coated [blueberries]{ ing="blueberries" } without overmixing.
1. Pour batter into liners—fill only 2/3 full. Bake 18-21 minutes until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. (Mini cupcakes: bake 11-13 minutes at same temperature.) Cool completely before frosting.
1. Beat [cream cheese]{ ing="full-fat-brick-cream-cheese" } and butter together on medium speed until smooth (about 2 minutes). Add confectioners’ sugar, vanilla, and salt; beat on low for 30 seconds, then increase to medium-high for 2 full minutes. Taste and adjust salt if desired. Refrigerate at least 20 minutes for intricate piping.
1. Frost cooled cupcakes and add optional garnish. Refrigerate decorated cupcakes uncovered for at least 20 minutes before serving.

## Notes

- Cover and store leftover cupcakes in the refrigerator for up to 5 days
